}{\plain \fs24 \b\f3 The Liturgy of the Palms}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 When circumstances permit, the congregation may gather at a place\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 apart from the church, so that all may go into the church in procession.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The branches of palm or of other trees or shrubs to be carried in the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 procession may be distributed to the people before the service, or after\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 the prayer of blessing.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The following or some other suitable anthem is sung or said, the people\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 standing\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  }{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Blessed is the King who comes in the name of the Lord.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Peace in heaven and glory in the highest.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3   \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Celebrant}{\plain \fs24 \f3     Let us pray.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Assist us mercifully with your help, O Lord God of our\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 salvation, that we may enter with joy upon the contemplation\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 of those mighty acts, whereby you have given us life and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 immortality; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Here a Deacon or other person appointed reads one of the following}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\column 
\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Year A}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20     Matthew 21:1-11 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Year B}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20     Mark 11:1-11 }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 or}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  John 12:12-16 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Year C}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20     Luke 19:28-40}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3   \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The Celebrant then says the following blessing\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs24\fi-990\li990\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Celebrant}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \ul0 \tab The Lord be with you. \par
}\pard \fs24\fi-990\li990\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 People}{\plain \fs24 \f3   \ul0 \tab And also with you. \par
}\pard \fs24\fi-990\li990\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Celebrant}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \ul0 \tab Let us give thanks to the Lord our God. \par
}\pard \fs24\fi-990\li990\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 People}{\plain \fs24 \f3   \ul0 \tab It is right to give him thanks and praise.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs24 \f3 It is right to praise you, Almighty God, for the acts of love by\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 which you have redeemed us through your Son Jesus Christ\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 our Lord. On this day he entered the holy city of Jerusalem in\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 triumph, and was proclaimed as King of kings by those who\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 spread their garments and branches of palm along his way.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Let these branches be for us signs of his victory, and grant that\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 we who bear them in his name may ever hail him as our King,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and follow him in the way that leads to eternal life; who lives\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and reigns in glory with you and the Holy Spirit, now and for \softline
ever. }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The following or some other suitable anthem may then be sung or said\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  }{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Hosanna in the highest.}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 The Procession\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs24 \i\f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\fi-990\li990\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Deacon}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \ul0 \tab Let us go forth in peace. \par
}\pard \fs24\fi-990\li990\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 People}{\plain \fs24 \f3   \ul0 \tab In the name of Christ.  Amen.\par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 During the procession, all hold branches in their hands, and\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 appropriate hymns, psalms, or anthems are sung, such as the hymn "All\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 glory, laid, and honor" and Psalm 118:19-29.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 At a suitable place, the procession may halt while the following or\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 some other appropriate Collect is said}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\column 
\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Almighty God, whose most dear Son went not up to joy but\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 first he suffered pain, and entered not into glory before he\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 was crucified: Mercifully grant that we, walking in the way\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 of the cross, may find it none other than the way of life and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 peace; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 In the absence of a bishop or priest, the preceding service may be led\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 by a deacon or lay reader.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 At services on this day other than the principal celebration, suitable\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 portions of the preceding may be used.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \b\f3 At the Eucharist}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 When the Liturgy of the Palms immediately precedes the Eucharist, the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 celebration begins with the Salutation and Collect of the Day.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Let us pray.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Almighty and everliving God, in your tender love for the\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 human race you sent your Son our Savior Jesus Christ to take\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 upon him our nature, and to suffer death upon the cross,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 giving us the example of his great humility: Mercifully grant\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 that we may walk in the way of his suffering, and also share\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 in his resurrection; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and ever.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen}{\plain \fs24 \f3 .\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Old Testament}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20    Isaiah 50:4-9a\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Psalm}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20    31:9-16\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Epistle}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20     Philippians 2:5-11 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The Passion Gospel is announced in the following manner}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs24 \f3 The Passion of our Lord Jesus Christ according to_________\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The customary responses before and after the Gospel are omitted.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\column 
\pard \fs20\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Year A}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20     Matthew 26:14-27:66   }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 or}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  27:11-54 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Year B}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20     Mark 14:1-15:47   }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 or}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  15:1-39(40-47) \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Year C}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20     Luke 22:14-23:56   }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 or}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  23:1-49\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The Passion Gospel may be read or chanted by different persons.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Specific roles may be assigned to different persons, the congregation\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 taking the part of the crowd.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The congregation may be seated for the first part of the Passion.  At\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 the verse which mentions the arrival at Golgotha (Matthew 27:33,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Mark 15:22, Luke 23:33) all stand.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 When the Liturgy of the Palms has preceded, the Nicene Creed and the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Confession of Sin may be omitted at this service.}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Preface of Holy Week\par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3  }{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\column 
\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs44 \f3\fs44 Maundy Thursday}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The Eucharist begins in the usual manner, using the following Collect,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Psalm, and Lessons}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Almighty Father, whose dear Son, on the night before\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 he suffered, instituted the Sacrament of his Body and Blood:\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Mercifully grant that we may receive it thankfully in\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 remembrance of Jesus Christ our Lord, who in these holy\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 mysteries gives us a pledge of eternal life; and who now lives\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and ever.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Old Testament}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20     Exodus 12:1-4(5-10)11-14 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Psalm}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20     116:1,10-17 (}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 omit Hallelujah in verse 17}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 )\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Epistle}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20     1 Corinthians 11:23-26 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Gospel}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20     John 13:1-17,31b-35\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20   \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 When observed, the ceremony of the washing of feet appropriately\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 follows the Gospel and homily.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 During the ceremony, the following or other words may be\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 sung or said}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 The Lord Jesus, after he had supped with his disciples and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 had washed their feet, said to them, {\u8220\'93}Do you know what I,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 your Lord and Master, have done to you?  I have given you\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 an example, that you should do as I have done.{\u8221\'94}\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Peace is my last gift to you, my own peace I now leave with\par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 you; peace which the world cannot give, I give to you.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs24 \f3 I give you a new commandment: Love one another as I have\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 loved you.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Peace is my last gift to you, my own peace I now leave with\par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 you; peace which the world cannot give, I give to you.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-1440\tx-720\tx0\tx360\tx990\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6010
{\plain \fs24 \f3 By this shall the world know that you are my disciples: That\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 you have love for one another.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The service continues with the Prayers of the People.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Where it is desired to administer Holy Communion from the reserved\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Sacrament on Good Friday, the Sacrament for that purpose is\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 consecrated at this service.}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3  \par
